     "quote": "A capo ( KAH-poh; short for capodastro, capo tasto, copypasto or capotasto [ˌkapoˈtasto], Italian for \"head of fretboard\") is a device a musician uses on the neck of a stringed (typically fretted) instrument to transpose and shorten the playable length of the strings—hence raising the pitch.",
